From 180aaf8cb969fe0262997a937d0cf0b67e950dc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:23:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/88] readwait: wait for data without a buffer on QUIC
 streams and gRPC lite

A connection that can wait for data without consuming it gets a read waiter
that waits first and takes the copy buffer only once data is there, then reads
through the connection's own Read: the TCP streams of Hysteria2 and TUIC and the
v2ray QUIC transport (quic-go Peek), and gRPC lite (Peek of its frame reader, at
the start of a message only: inside one a read goes past the reader's 4 KiB
buffer to the body).

Idle Hysteria2 connection, live heap: 37 -> 5 KiB after a short response,
70 -> 5 KiB after a bulk transfer; gRPC: 63 -> 30 KiB and 99 -> 33 KiB.
